        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{5}{33}$",
          "worked": "Let $S=0.\\dot{1}\\dot{5}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}100S&=15.1515\\ldots\\\\100S&=15+S\\\\99S&=15\\\\S&=\\frac{15}{99}\\\\S&=\\frac{5}{33}\\end{align*}$$\nThe numerator and denominator are integers and the denominator is nonzero, so the number is rational.",
